<h1>Credits &amp; licences</h1>
<p>
  <%= SITE_NAME %> is built entirely from freely-licensed data. Because KanjiVG is
  share-alike (CC BY-SA), this site&rsquo;s derived database and pages are offered
  under <strong>CC BY-SA</strong> as well.
</p>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>KanjiVG</h2>
  <p>Stroke-order paths and component / radical decomposition.</p>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>Author</dt><dd><%= meta.kanjivg_attribution %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd><%= meta.kanjivg_license %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Source</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/KanjiVG/kanjivg">github.com/KanjiVG/kanjivg</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>KANJIDIC2</h2>
  <p>Meanings, on&rsquo;yomi / kun&rsquo;yomi readings, stroke counts, radical numbers, grade and frequency.</p>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd><%= meta.kanjidic2_attribution %> (Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group)</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd><%= meta.kanjidic2_license %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Version</dt><dd>file <%= meta.kanjidic2_file_version %>, database <%= meta.kanjidic2_database_version %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Source</dt><dd><a href="https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project">edrdg.org — KANJIDIC Project</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="note">
    The SKIP code field in KANJIDIC2 is licensed CC BY-NC-SA (non-commercial) and
    is deliberately <strong>not used</strong> anywhere in this project.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>JMdict</h2>
  <p>Example words (jukugo) — the common words shown on each kanji page, with readings and glosses.</p>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>Publisher</dt><dd><%= meta.jmdict_attribution || 'EDRDG / Jim Breen' %> (Electronic Dictionary Research and Development Group)</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd><%= meta.jmdict_license || 'CC BY-SA 4.0' %></dd></div>
    <% if (meta.jmdict_date) { %><div><dt>Version</dt><dd><%= meta.jmdict_date %> (common-words subset)</dd></div><% } %>
    <div><dt>Source</dt><dd><a href="https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project">edrdg.org — JMdict/EDICT</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
</section>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>KRADFILE / RADKFILE</h2>
  <p>Kanji ↔ component decomposition — powers the radical picker and the &ldquo;shares components&rdquo; links.</p>
  <dl>
    <div><dt>Author</dt><dd><%= meta.krad_attribution || 'James Breen / EDRDG' %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Licence</dt><dd><%= meta.krad_license || 'CC BY-SA 3.0' %></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Source</dt><dd><a href="https://www.edrdg.org/krad/kradinf.html">edrdg.org — RADKFILE/KRADFILE</a></dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p class="note">
    JMdict, KRADFILE and RADKFILE are used here via the JSON conversion published by
    <a href="https://github.com/scriptin/jmdict-simplified">jmdict-simplified</a> (scriptin).
  </p>
</section>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>Origin stories</h2>
  <p>
    The plain-language origin explanations are generated by Anthropic&rsquo;s Claude
    (Haiku) from the component and meaning data above. They are convenience
    summaries, not scholarship, and may be wrong — each page marks whether its
    story has been human-reviewed.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="credit">
  <h2>Other</h2>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/WaniKani/WanaKana">WanaKana</a> (MIT) converts romaji search input to kana.</p>
  <p>Database built <%= meta.build_timestamp %>.</p>
</section>

<%- include('partials/foot', { pageClass: 'page-credits' }) %>
